<title>CHINA: Southeast Asia Prop yr net off 16.27 pct.</title>
<headline>Southeast Asia Prop yr net off 16.27 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   3.8	 vs 4.5</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    2.0	 vs 2.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  0.43 gain vs 2.34 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    4.50	vs 5.37</p>
<p>    Turnover		     149.18    vs 157.85 (see note)</p>
<p>    Company name		 Southeast Asia Properties &amp; Finance</p>
<p>				     Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  September 15-20</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   October 14</p>
<p>NOTE - Southeast Asia is a property development and investment company.</p>
<p>Comparative turnover has been reclassified to conform with the current year's presentation.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$7.75 million on disposal of long term listed investments, loss of HK$5.03 million from interest incurred on suspended properties under development, loss of HK$0.94 million on diminution in value of property under development, loss of HK$0.12 million from long term unlisted investment written off and loss of HK$1.23 million on severance payments.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is two H.K. cents vs four cents.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
